{
  "case_id": "2008-08-598",
  "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Three separate lines of double jeopardy analysis lead independently to the conclusion that the Double Jeopardy Clause commits the Ohio postconviction court to hold a hearing to determine whether Mr. Bies is mentally retarded for purposes of Atkins."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There has been no acquittal in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But even -- even if that's so, that's not necessarily an -- an Atkins finding, isn't that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was an admission; it couldn't have been a finding of fact. You said that that's what the State claimed. Where is the admission of the State in this State postconviction proceeding that Mr. Bies is mentally retarded?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The defendant is shown by the record to be mildly mentally retarded with an IQ of 69."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it primarily does raise a question of judicial estoppel, which we raised, which is -- and that is not a technical basis on which to grant habeas. It is a reason that the writ should be dismissed as improvidently granted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I'm not sure that there's even anything -- I mean, it does raise a judicial estoppel issue, but I'm not sure there is a -- a record hereupon which a -- a judicial estoppel claim could be maintained, because in the passages that you referred us to, first the State's concession and secondly the finding which -- which followed from it, it was a reference to mild mental retardation and a specific reference to an IQ of 69."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The very next sentence is as a matter of law -- the law as it was then -- such a person may be punished by execution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-598",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aed7b430a66a00ec606625ba7523a4caf9fe4b72b01677d4777e8f1965762fa5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aed7b430a66a-0002-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
